The  utility  traverses  the  directories  containing  man pages,
parses the manual pages with the help of  and  builds  an  SQLite
database  to support full text searches by It obtains the list of
directories to traverse using the option of It supports the  fol‐
lowing  options:  Use  different  configuration file than the de‐
fault, Force rebuilding the index from scratch, pruning  the  ex‐
isting  one.   Limit  the parsing to only the NAME section of the
pages.  This option can be used to  mimic  the  behavior  of  the
classic  and also to substantially save disk space.  Use this op‐
tion to optimize the index for faster search by and also to  sig‐
nificantly reduce disk space usage.  This is an expensive I/O op‐
eration.   Print  only fatal error messages (i.e., when the data‐
base is left in an inconsistent state and needs manual  interven‐
tion).   Print only warnings and error messages but no status up‐
dates.  Enable verbose output.  This prints  the  name  of  every
file  being  parsed and a summary at the end of the index update.
The index generated by is also used by the program, replacing the
old program.  The name of the FTS table is mandb and  its  schema
is  as follows: page is relevant.  The location of the SQLite FTS
database can be configured using the tag.
